Is the model actually executing on a NeuronCore in `bfloat16` — weights and caches on the `neuron` device, the hot path in `torch.compile(backend="neuron")` regions — and not silently running on CPU or in `float32`? Look for eager CPU fallbacks (`torch_neuronx.get_fallback_ops()` listing hot-path ops), `TORCH_NEURONX_DISABLE_FALLBACK_EXECUTION=0`, or tensors left on CPU. A server that loads but falls back to CPU is incorrect for this target.
